{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"7180a2783c257f6496be0c5ad03589e811edfeec028bb45665b0332e0df47165","packTokens":2181,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":357,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":705,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":981,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"When an invoice is 7 days past its due date, the system shall mark it overdue and show it on the overdue list\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"When staff press 'Send reminder' on an overdue invoice, the system shall email the customer a reminder with the invoice number, amount and due date\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"The system shall record each reminder sent, with who sent it and when, and show the history on the invoice\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"If an email cannot be delivered, the system shall show the failure on the invoice and keep it on the overdue list\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Staff shall be able to filter the overdue list by customer and by days overdue\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Build overdue list screen (table, filters, a 'Send reminder' button per row)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Build invoice detail screen (amount, due date, reminder history, delivery failures)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Who can view the screens and send reminders, and how do staff sign in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any authenticated staff user, using the existing API's authentication\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which email address receives the reminder, and what happens if the customer has several contacts or none?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The customer's single billing email from the existing record; if missing, the send is blocked with an error\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Can reminder history entries be edited or deleted?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No, they are append-only and immutable\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope. So how does an invoice come off the overdue list once it is paid or closed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"The existing system's invoice status (paid/cancelled) is read and closed invoices drop off automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How should repeated sends be guarded against?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Disable the button while a send is in progress only\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Is 'overdue' a status saved on the invoice (for example by a daily job), or is it worked out from the due date each time the list loads?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Computed at query time from due date and today's date\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where are reminder history records stored, given that invoices live in the client's existing system?\",\n  \"answer\": \"New table in the same Postgres database, referencing invoice ID\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Is a failed send recorded in the append-only reminder history, and does a later successful send clear the failure shown on the invoice?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt (success or failure) is a history entry; the latest status is shown\",\n  \"by\": \"mhamza\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The system shall compute, on every request without ever persisting the result, whether an invoice is overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice is overdue only if its status is in a configured list of open statuses that has no default value and must be set at deployment.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice with a null due date is never classified as overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice is overdue when the number of calendar days from its due date to today, computed in a configured business time zone, is at least a configured overdue threshold that defaults to 7.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the API shall return every invoice currently classified as overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Each returned overdue invoice shall include its invoice ID, invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, and days overdue calculated as calendar days since the due date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter, the API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue fall within the named fixed bucket: 7-30, 31-60, or 61+, with limits inclusive.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"These bucket boundaries are fixed and are not shifted by the configured overdue threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"If the requested bucket value is not one of the three defined buckets, the API shall respond 400 with a validation error identifying the bucket parameter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"If a request to any Invoice Reminders endpoint lacks a valid authentication token, the API shall reject it with HTTP 401 without returning invoice data, sending email, or changing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"If a request carries a valid, unexpired token that lacks the configured staff claim, the API shall reject it with HTTP 403 without returning invoice or customer data or changing data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"The staff claim type and value used for this check are configurable, with no built-in default value.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint shall meet stated latency requirements at stated data volumes, with or without filters applied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Customer PII, specifically billing email addresses, and invoice amounts shall be kept out of application logs.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"All Invoice Reminders endpoints shall require staff authentication.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}